// THE ESCAPED CLOSURE CALLED OUTSIDE ANY INSTALL (the root gate reads the
// row alone, 2026-09-27). E rides the closure's value row out of `escaped`;
// the bare call at main performs it with no enclosing install, so E is in
// main's row and the executable refuses (E_EffectUnhandled). The boot
// accepted this program because h was installed SOMEWHERE, and the call
// aborted at the runtime walk (exit 134) — sound-escape-birth-evidence's
// old premise, the "static singleton" direct call, described tiers that no
// longer exist. Its sound twin calls the escaped closure under h.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(1) }
fn make() = () => op()
fn escaped() = (make()) ~> h
fn main() = escaped()()
